(4843472, 700717, 63503, '<td valign="top">Depth of field is impressive here, as this cannot be only a wide angle shot that was cropped,so, I would guess at least 150 to 200 mm focal length, that would require a very small aperture for this kind of dof (f22 or bigger?) which leaves me with the doubt about the ISO, it would have to be very high since the moon does not show motion blur, but then, there is no noise at all and the moon does not look ''nija''d out''!!!. Lots of un-answered questions and I can''t wait to see yur settings. Great shot.</td>', 'Depth of field is impressive here, as this cannot be only a wide angle shot that was cropped,so, I would guess at least 150 to 200 mm focal length, that would require a very small aperture for this kind of dof (f22 or bigger?) which leaves me with the doubt about the ISO, it would have to be very high since the moon does not show motion blur, but then, there is no noise at all and the moon does not look ''nija''d out''!!!. Lots of un-answered questions and I can''t wait to see yur settings. Great shot.', '2008-07-24 20:04:51.000000', NULL, 1),
