(4851045, 701928, 67152, '<td valign="top">Okay lady...Now you are showing off! <br/> <br/>Great stuff - love the ice and fire all at once.  How long did it take you to decide which of the two challenges to enter?</td>', 'Okay lady...Now you are showing off!  Great stuff - love the ice and fire all at once.  How long did it take you to decide which of the two challenges to enter?', '2008-07-30 08:19:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851050, 699986, 41337, '<td valign="top">Very nice light and tones in this photo. I''m surprised this got that many 3s but looking at the rest of the vote distribution it has a classic bell curve to it, which at DPC usually means "good shot" but lack wow factor. You almost have it here in the light and in the tones but a couple of things let you down. First the color, I understand the green connection with 7up but it doesn''t help to convey coldness very well and since you''re not shooting for that company but rather people who just want to see coldness a blue color would have been better. The other thing is there is a total lack of energy in the photo. When you look at beverage ads they almost always have movement, water splashes or at the very least drops of water on the can. That helps make the product more appealing and I think voters have come to expect that in these types of shots. Had you done that those 5 votes would have been 6s, 7s and 8s and you''d be seeing a much different score.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-30 07:23:55.</i></td>', 'Very nice light and tones in this photo. I''m surprised this got that many 3s but looking at the rest of the vote distribution it has a classic bell curve to it, which at DPC usually means "good shot" but lack wow factor. You almost have it here in the light and in the tones but a couple of things let you down. First the color, I understand the green connection with 7up but it doesn''t help to convey coldness very well and since you''re not shooting for that company but rather people who just want to see coldness a blue color would have been better. The other thing is there is a total lack of energy in the photo. When you look at beverage ads they almost always have movement, water splashes or at the very least drops of water on the can. That helps make the product more appealing and I think voters have come to expect that in these types of shots. Had you done that those 5 votes would have been 6s, 7s and 8s and you''d be seeing a much different score.', '2008-07-30 08:22:05.000000', '2008-07-30 08:23:55.000000', 0),
(4851052, 701518, 77746, '<td valign="top">rokk og ról elskan!<br/> <br/>vá hvað þú hefur fengið ÆÐIS dag þarna!</td>', 'rokk og ról elskan! vá hvað þú hefur fengið ÆÐIS dag þarna!', '2008-07-30 08:23:14.000000', NULL, 0),
