(4867004, 701518, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>What''s not to like? :)  It is a lovely scene that fits the challenge extraordinarily well.<br/> <br/>The only little nitpick and it obviously didn''t affect your score negatively, is that your horizon is completely in the middle.  While this affords a nice view of both the sky and water, moving it up or down might have made it feel more dramatic.<br/> <br/>THAT SAID, I think this image exemplifies how the "rules" of photography can be broken and still be a wonderful, strong image.<br/> <br/>Great image and congrats on your ribbon.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat What''s not to like? :)  It is a lovely scene that fits the challenge extraordinarily well. The only little nitpick and it obviously didn''t affect your score negatively, is that your horizon is completely in the middle.  While this affords a nice view of both the sky and water, moving it up or down might have made it feel more dramatic. THAT SAID, I think this image exemplifies how the "rules" of photography can be broken and still be a wonderful, strong image. Great image and congrats on your ribbon. Karma', '2008-08-05 15:09:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4867324, 701784, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE <br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Overall, I think you have met the challenge in an obvious enough fashion.  The visible thumprint is actually a neat touch (no pun intended) and adds a bit of interest and "story" to the shot.  (again, no pun intended).<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I like how it "fills" the frame, but it seems a bit static to me.  There is really nowhere for the eyes to "go," or anything to see except the glass.  As a result, the dpc voter probalby looked, said, "Cold glass," voted and moved on.  Perhaps a more dramatic angle or perspective would have helped to add interest.  As it is now, I feel like I am almost eye level with the glass, maybe a touch above, and while this is a natural viewing level, it doesn''t add to the interest much at all.  Also, the crop is just a touch off so it is not symmetrical, though it feels it should be.<br/> <br/>technically, I think the bw is a good choice for this.  the focus and exposure are very good.<br/> <br/>Again, I think you had a good idea, and you executed it well, technically, but the composition leaves it a bit "ho-hum" and doesn''t compel the viewer to stay with it long.</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE by karmat Overall, I think you have met the challenge in an obvious enough fashion.  The visible thumprint is actually a neat touch (no pun intended) and adds a bit of interest and "story" to the shot.  (again, no pun intended). Compositionally, I like how it "fills" the frame, but it seems a bit static to me.  There is really nowhere for the eyes to "go," or anything to see except the glass.  As a result, the dpc voter probalby looked, said, "Cold glass," voted and moved on.  Perhaps a more dramatic angle or perspective would have helped to add interest.  As it is now, I feel like I am almost eye level with the glass, maybe a touch above, and while this is a natural viewing level, it doesn''t add to the interest much at all.  Also, the crop is just a touch off so it is not symmetrical, though it feels it should be. technically, I think the bw is a good choice for this.  the focus and exposure are very good. Again, I think you had a good idea, and you executed it well, technically, but the composition leaves it a bit "ho-hum" and doesn''t compel the viewer to stay with it long.', '2008-08-05 17:25:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4867510, 702071, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Juliane,<br/> <br/>This is a nice capture but it really does not convey that Stone Cold look. I think this is do to the eyes and the overall facial expression. It looks more like Im sorry forgive me type look. Also it looks to me that from between his eyes &amp; up across the right side of his forehead are a bit hot. I do like the use of the black sheets this was a nice idea. The one distraction to the image is that upper right corner, the brown immediately catches the eye. Overall you have a nice image. It has interest and the tonality is well done. I think with a few minor ajustments it could be outstanding.   <br/></td>', 'Hi Juliane, This is a nice capture but it really does not convey that Stone Cold look. I think this is do to the eyes and the overall facial expression. It looks more like Im sorry forgive me type look. Also it looks to me that from between his eyes & up across the right side of his forehead are a bit hot. I do like the use of the black sheets this was a nice idea. The one distraction to the image is that upper right corner, the brown immediately catches the eye. Overall you have a nice image. It has interest and the tonality is well done. I think with a few minor ajustments it could be outstanding.   ', '2008-08-05 19:07:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4867540, 702184, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Steff,<br/> <br/>       First let me say that this is a very nice image. You did a great job on the highlights &amp; midtones. The blurring of the falls is also nicely done. Everything looks nice and sharp with good lighting. The composition is good with one little exception, top just right of center you caught someones legs tho off in the backgroud they did catch my eye. I also see a bit of blow-out on the bottom of the upper falls. As I mentioned before you did a great job with the highlights &amp; midtones but there is a lack of detail in some of the shadows. As far as the challenge &amp; title go, it works for me. An overall lovely capture.</td>', 'Hi Steff,        First let me say that this is a very nice image. You did a great job on the highlights & midtones. The blurring of the falls is also nicely done. Everything looks nice and sharp with good lighting. The composition is good with one little exception, top just right of center you caught someones legs tho off in the backgroud they did catch my eye. I also see a bit of blow-out on the bottom of the upper falls. As I mentioned before you did a great job with the highlights & midtones but there is a lack of detail in some of the shadows. As far as the challenge & title go, it works for me. An overall lovely capture.', '2008-08-05 19:34:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4867582, 702218, 96351, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8 during the challenge. Not sure why anyone would consider giving a 5 let alone anything under. She looks like an ice princess.</td>', 'I gave this an 8 during the challenge. Not sure why anyone would consider giving a 5 let alone anything under. She looks like an ice princess.', '2008-08-05 20:10:32.000000', NULL, 0),
